Subject: [PATCH 0/1] U9: runner provenance manifest (base science/p0-correctness-2026-10-19 @ ebc1fd79)

U9 (Round-11): runner provenance, delivered as a patch with a
demonstration manifest.

What it adds (base science/p0-correctness-2026-10-19 @ ebc1fd79):
- build_provenance_manifest() / write_provenance_manifest(): a standalone
  provenance record composing engine provenance (code_sha + tree state),
  sanitized git context (credential-stripped remotes, branch, describe),
  runtime (python + implementation + platform), material dependency
  versions (numpy/gemmi; explicitly 'unavailable' when missing), and the
  policy-binding hashes (canon, law semantic, modality matrix).
- --emit-provenance PATH CLI: writes the manifest and exits 0 without
  running a calibration; records tree state instead of refusing it.
- run_manifest.json now also carries the git block and dependencies.

Demonstration manifest: runner_provenance_demo.json (same directory) was
produced by running the committed patch itself:
  python3 backend/calibration/runner.py --emit-provenance <path>
It records code_sha f2a87fea... (this patch, clean tree), sanitized
remotes, Python 3.12.15/CPython, numpy 2.1.3, gemmi 0.7.5, and the
policy hashes.

Tests: backend/tests/test_runner_provenance.py (6 tests) plus the
existing runner suites (test_runner_hardening.py,
test_calibration_runner.py, 11 tests) — all passing in this environment
on commit f2a87fe.

Patch only; merge is owner-gated. No secrets appear in any artifact
(PAT used for the evidence push is never written to any file).


